{%- comment -%}
  won-unit-price — the ONE place the theme turns a price into a unit price.

  A unit price is a claim about a reference amount the shop actually knows. When
  that amount cannot be read, this snippet renders NOTHING: an invented number
  under a "/ 100 g" label is worse than no number at all (EshopAudit PRC-001).

  THE LADDER lives in one global theme setting, `won_unit_price_rules`, so a
  client can extend it without touching code. One rule per line:

      won.net_weight_g | 100 | t:won.unit.per_100g
      won.volume_ml    | 100 | 100 ml
      won.washes       | 1   | prací dávka
      # a line starting with '#' is parked and skipped

  <metafield namespace.key> | <how many units the price is quoted per> | <label>

  Rules are tried in order; the first whose metafield yields a positive number
  wins, and unit price = price x <units> / <metafield value>. A `t:` label goes
  through the locale files, anything else prints literally — that is what makes
  the list universal rather than "grams and servings".

  Only metafield paths are accepted. A literal amount would apply one made-up
  quantity to the whole catalogue, which is the defect this snippet exists to stop.

  Each rule is read PER VARIANT first, then per product. That order is not
  optional: a product with a size or count axis carries its weight/servings on the
  variant precisely because a product-level value would lie, so reading only
  `product.metafields` comes back blank on every such product.

  Params:
    product  (required)
    variant  optional; defaults to the selected/first available variant
    rules    optional per-section override of the global ladder, same syntax
    prefix   optional label, markup format only
    format   'markup' (default) | 'text'
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign wup_variant = variant | default: product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign wup_price = wup_variant.price
  if wup_price == blank
    assign wup_price = product.price
  endif

  assign wup_src = rules
  if wup_src == blank
    assign wup_src = settings.won_unit_price_rules
  endif
  # Liquid has no newline literal to split on; this is the canonical workaround.
  assign wup_lines = wup_src | newline_to_br | split: '<br />'

  assign wup_value = 0
  assign wup_label = ''

  for wup_line in wup_lines
    # A '#' line is a parked rule, documented in the setting's help text.
    assign wup_trimmed = wup_line | strip
    if wup_trimmed == blank
      continue
    endif
    assign wup_first = wup_trimmed | slice: 0
    if wup_first == '#'
      continue
    endif
    assign wup_parts = wup_line | split: '|'
    if wup_parts.size < 3
      continue
    endif
    assign wup_path = wup_parts[0] | strip
    assign wup_per = wup_parts[1] | strip | plus: 0
    assign wup_raw_label = wup_parts[2] | strip
    if wup_path == blank or wup_per <= 0 or wup_raw_label == blank
      continue
    endif

    assign wup_nk = wup_path | split: '.'
    if wup_nk.size < 2
      continue
    endif
    assign wup_ns = wup_nk[0]
    assign wup_key = wup_nk[1]
    assign wup_raw = wup_variant.metafields[wup_ns][wup_key].value
    if wup_raw == blank
      assign wup_raw = product.metafields[wup_ns][wup_key].value
    endif
    # `| plus: 0` coerces a text metafield to a number and a missing one to 0,
    # so a string value never silently fails a `> 0` comparison.
    assign wup_amount = wup_raw | plus: 0
    if wup_amount <= 0
      continue
    endif

    assign wup_value = wup_price | times: wup_per | divided_by: wup_amount
    if wup_raw_label contains 't:'
      assign wup_key_label = wup_raw_label | remove_first: 't:'
      assign wup_label = wup_key_label | t
    else
      assign wup_label = wup_raw_label
    endif
    break
  endfor
-%}
{%- if wup_value > 0 and wup_label != blank -%}
  {%- if format == 'text' -%}
    {{- wup_value | money }} / {{ wup_label -}}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- if prefix != blank -%}<span class="won-ppu__prefix">{{ prefix }}</span>{%- endif -%}
    <span class="won-ppu__value">{{ wup_value | money }}</span>
    <span class="won-ppu__unit">/ {{ wup_label }}</span>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
